### Task: Migrate Legacy HTML and CSS to Angular Components

We are continuing the migration of a vanilla JavaScript 3D Knowledge Graph into an Angular architecture. The TypeScript logic is now working, but the UI lacks the original aesthetic. 

I will provide the legacy `index.html` and `styles.css`. Your task is to distribute the HTML structure and CSS styles into the correct Angular components.

#### Global / Root Setup
1. **`src/index.html`**:
   - Add the Google Fonts links (`Inter`, `JetBrains Mono`, `Orbitron`).
   - Add the `.hologram-overlay` div inside the body (or inside `app.component.html`).
2. **`src/styles.scss`**:
   - Move the `:root` variables (e.g., `--hud-cyan`, `--hud-dark`).
   - Move the `body` and `*` resets.
   - Move `.hologram-overlay` and `@keyframes pulse` animations.

#### Component Mapping Instructions
Transfer the specific CSS classes and HTML layouts to their respective Angular components. **Do not change the Angular TypeScript logic or state bindings**, just update the templates (`.html`) and styles (`.scss` / `styles: []`).

1. **`app.component` (Top Bar & Controls)**:
   - Apply the `#hud-topbar`, `.hud-logo`, `.pulse-dot`, and `.hud-status` layout to the top bar.
   - Apply the `#controls-hud` and `.recenter-btn` styles to the bottom-left controls.
2. **`graph-search.component`**:
   - Apply `.hud-search-container`, `.hud-search-input`, `.hud-search-badge`.
   - Style the dropdown using `.hud-search-results`, `.search-result-item`, `.search-item-header`, `.search-item-title`, `.search-item-type`, and `.search-item-summary`.
3. **`graph-inspector.component` (Side Panel)**:
   - Map the `#info-panel` container styles, including the `clip-path` and backdrop filters.
   - Style the header and tabs using `.panel-header`, `.panel-title`, `.panel-code`, `.panel-nav-btn`, `.panel-toggle-btn`, `.tabs`, and `.tab-btn`.
   - Style the content details using `.property`, `.prop-title`, `.value-box`, `.signature-box`, `.pill-list`, `.pill-item`, `.tag-container`, and `.tag`.
   - Move all the `.markdown-rendered` nested rules (h1, h2, pre, code, blockquote, table) so the markdown docs render perfectly.
   - *Note:* Implement the `#info-panel.is-collapsed` behavior using an Angular `[class.is-collapsed]="isCollapsed"` binding and a toggle button.
4. **`graph-hud.component` (Screen-space Overlay)**:
   - Apply `.hud-labels-layer`, `.hud-floating-pill`, `.hud-floating-pill.is-target`, and `.hud-cluster-badge` styles. Ensure the `span` within the badge gets its specific styling.

#### Execution
1. Read the provided legacy `index.html` and `styles.css`.
2. Update the `.ts` files (if using inline styles/templates) or `.html`/`.scss` files for each component listed above.
3. Ensure no global CSS bleeds into unintended components (use Angular's default ViewEncapsulation where appropriate, but put `.markdown-rendered` global overrides in a way that affects dynamically injected HTML).
4. Run the build to ensure no template errors were introduced.